"Knights are wizards sworn to grow their power and protect the Triplanets from chaos and demons."
"They rank above all regular wizards; not always the strongest, but never weak."
"A knight may not break the sacred promise, and knights are not family to one another."
"Fighting a knight means execution by beheading, even for the winner."
"Knights carry ordinal titles: the Primary, the only one and most powerful, then secondary, tertiary."
"The Primary's role is something like a cross between a nuclear warhead and the Pope."
"Artonans say brave matters more than strong for a knight."
"Worli Ro-den calls knighthood a terrible life for crazy wizards and idiots."
"Knights are the Triplanets' first line of defense, so high-ranked humans are rarely sent to fight."
"Knights bind their authority into skills like Avowed, but are not Avowed, and feel the binding."
"A knight funnels power into one well-designed, infinitely expandable skill plus a few conveniences."
"Knights wear metal studs instead of embroidery and use the System without tablets or lenses."
"A knight on duty must have a healer at all times."
"Knights may choose their rest, a final sacrifice, to escape the pain of affixation."
"The Primary releases them by holding their hands; they fall dead without a mark."
"Released knights' authority is woven into ground and forest as a ward against chaos."
"Knights once included non-Artonans, but do not recruit humans."
"Knight students wear quilted purple coats and enter training around human age twelve."
"Earth's System renders the numbered knights as Generals; the Quaternary is the Fourth General."
"Seeing a numbered knight is like sighting an endangered animal."
"Wizards are obliged to keep silent about knights outside their class."
"Knights live in Privately Governed Territories on Artona I, such as the forest Knight Rapport 1."
"Even Artonans cannot affix without swearing oaths never to harm the Triplanets."
"Knights are addressed by title on first meeting until they give permission to stop."
"Earth's System renders the knight title differently than Artona I and III do."
"Two knights monitor and back up the battle group at Matadero; Earth is a comfortable posting."
"A knight can ask the Contract for an injury assessment of an Avowed, or confirm deaths."
"Knight Lind-otta's pacification slows motion, not time, across a huge area."
"Artonans keep a respectful silence about a knight's authority being bound into a skill."
"Publicly, knights are said to cast spells; they are hard to catch on film using magic."
"Earth news calls knights generals, of the Mother Planet's anti-chaos force."
"The knight path is called the path of highest onus; those who walk it share a communion."
"Knights are ranked by number; Iella-inwer was sixty-eighth, the Primary and Alis first and fourth."
"New knights, newlings, form squads; the early years are hardest and people are lost unexpectedly."
"Many knights die during their first binding or within a few years, especially in bad cycles."
"Knight families' children have abnormally strong bodies; most become knights or votaries."
"Knights hold the Mother privilege: asking Artona I's Contract to break a rule for them."
"Artona I grants it by weighing how much the knight has given, taken, and what is asked."
"Knights use many wordchains; chaotic environments cut their efficacy, needing many casts."
"Knights may eventually have their fingers altered, as one option among enhancements."
"Young knights outrank elder wizards and get privileges wizards receive only after graduation."
"Knight uniforms enhance physical abilities; wooden shoulder pins carved with skill symbols honor them."
"Most knights attend DawnStep university, known for its magnificent laboratories."
"Newling squads are formed deliberately, partly to help members find a partner to deepen with."
"There are more than forty-five thousand knights; about 1,600 to 1,700 join in a year."
"Of about 1,235 heading to first binding in a year, some seventy delay or change paths, few from Rapports."
"Outsider knights die faster early on and first serve in larger, swapping groups or in pairs."
"For the past three years young knights have mainly been sent to the corrupted planet Goldbush."
"Every knight holds that repairing as much reality from chaos as possible is necessary."
